{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 his father Raymond II was the Count of Tripoli and his mother Hodierna was the daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem. Raymond III became the Count of Tripoli after his father's death in 1152. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during his reign he was a member of the Haute Cour and participated in several battles against the Muslim forces. In 1164 Raymond III was taken prisoner by Nur ad-Din the emir of Aleppo during a battle he was released in 1173 after paying a large ransom. \n*Relationships and Alliances* \nRaymond III formed alliances with other Christian leaders in the region including King Amalric I of Jerusalem and the Knights Templar. He also formed alliances with Muslim leaders including Nur ad-Din and Saladin. Raymond III was a key player in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 where the Christian forces defeated the Muslim army. \n*Later Life and Death* \nRaymond III died in 1187 his death led to a succession crisis in the County of Tripoli. He was succeeded by Raymond IV Count of Tripoli who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch and Orgueilleuse of Harcourt. Raymond III's legacy was significant he played a crucial role in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \n*Capture and Release* \nRaymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din in 1164 and was released in 1173 after paying a large ransom. This event had a significant impact on his life and reign as the Count of Tripoli. \n*Battle of Hattin* \nRaymond III also played a role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Christian forces were defeated by the Muslim army led by Saladin. This battle marked the beginning of the end of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and had a significant impact on the history of the region.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009116546134464443}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00019631843315437436}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.16799601912498474}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.5130591988563538}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -6.437280717364047e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.05910847708582878}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -2.145764938177308e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.0052352952770888805}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -3.3378546504536644e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.13372428715229034}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.010658834129571915}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.16065005958080292}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.06497925519943237}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -8.702239938429557e-06}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.041907183825969696}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -4.0649541915627196e-05}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -0.0009182051289826632}, {"token": "erna", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": -7.438383181579411e-05}, {"token": "